<ArticleTitle>Low glycaemic index diet versus usual care for preventing type 2 diabetes in Indian adults with prediabetes: a randomised trial</ArticleTitle><Abstract><AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">South Asian adults have high diabetes risk.</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="METHODS">We randomised n = 240 adults with prediabetes to a low glycaemic index diet or usual care. Participants were followed with standardised dietary assessment and outcomes were ascertained by trained staff blinded to allocation where applicable. </AbstractText><AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Diabetes incidence was lower with the intervention.</AbstractText><AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS">A low GI diet reduced progression.</AbstractText></Abstract><Language>eng</Language><GrantList><Grant><Agency>Indian Council of Medical Research</Agency><Country>India</Country></Grant></GrantList><PublicationTypeList><PublicationType>Journal Article</PublicationType><PublicationType>Randomized Controlled Trial</PublicationType></PublicationTypeList></Article>
